<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Sammel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1544</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Giri-Sumel</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Sammel was fought in January 1544 near Sammel in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a> between the army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sher-shah-suri">Sher Shah Suri</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rathore">Rathore</a> forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rao-maldeo">Rao Maldeo</a> of Marwar. Maldeo withdrew before the battle, but his commanders Jaita and Kumpa attacked and were killed after heavy fighting. Sher Shah won but is said to have remarked that he had nearly lost the empire for a handful of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/millet">millet</a>.</p></div>
